WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.535 --> 00:00:05.087
Finding a feature shouldn't mean searching through dozens of files.

2
00:00:05.529 --> 00:00:09.592
Meet Group Code, the Visual Studio Code extension that organizes

3
00:00:09.639 --> 00:00:11.612
your codebase by what it does.

4
00:00:12.216 --> 00:00:13.923
Start with a simple comment.

5
00:00:14.248 --> 00:00:17.754
Add an at-group annotation above your code, give it a

6
00:00:17.824 --> 00:00:20.018
name, and describe its purpose.

7
00:00:20.622 --> 00:00:24.709
Use the greater-than separator to create a hierarchy, like Checkout,

8
00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:25.986
then Payments.

9
00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:28.610
Your groups appear in the sidebar.

10
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.765
Related code can live in TypeScript, SQL, or HTML, while

11
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.866
still belonging to the same feature.

12
00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:40.034
Expand a feature to explore all of its source files.

13
00:00:40.475 --> 00:00:42.937
Click a group to jump straight to its code.

14
00:00:43.448 --> 00:00:46.338
Search to narrow the list, and favorite the groups you

15
00:00:46.455 --> 00:00:47.418
use most.

16
00:00:47.859 --> 00:00:49.264
Need to reorganize?

17
00:00:49.775 --> 00:00:53.501
Rename a parent group, and its child annotations follow.

18
00:00:54.105 --> 00:00:57.217
Your edits stay available for review and undo.

19
00:00:57.727 --> 00:01:01.594
For a faster starting point, the Copilot integration can suggest

20
00:01:01.663 --> 00:01:02.929
group annotations.

21
00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:06.899
Review the proposed changes, then save when you're ready.

22
00:01:07.503 --> 00:01:10.417
Group Code keeps its index up to date as eligible

23
00:01:10.463 --> 00:01:14.620
files change, and respects your workspace's ignore rules.

24
00:01:15.223 --> 00:01:17.522
Turn a collection of files into a map of your

25
00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:18.381
features.

26
00:01:18.764 --> 00:01:22.236
Find Group Code in the Visual Studio Code Marketplace.
